{
  "$comment": [
    "The common envelope's cases (context/layers.md, \"Common envelope\"), stated once for every system tool",
    "and for docproc: docproc-ooxml's tests, the shared Rust crate's, and docproc's internal/cli's read this",
    "file in place, so no language restates a case. A case is added here, never in one tool's tests.",
    "exit_codes: each exit code and its meaning.",
    "warnings: a warning's where and what as the tool has them, and the stderr line it writes for them, its",
    "  tool's name spelled \"tool\"; split at its first three \": \" and unescaped, the line gives them back.",
    "errors: an error's reason and the stderr line it writes for it, its tool's name spelled \"tool\".",
    "media_names: a payload's bytes, in lowercase hex, and the name it is stored under, and the media name",
    "  they make: the bytes' lowercase hex SHA-256, then \".\" and the stored extension when that is 1 to 8",
    "  ASCII letters and digits.",
    "literal_escape: a line of literal text and its Markdown; no case holds a line break."
  ],
